  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "The big U – passing at speed over the whole rink",
  "description": "One line at the centre line and a fixed passer (X) in each corner on the same long side. A skates without the puck up towards the corner, gets a pass from the passer and plays it straight back. A curves out towards the board and gets the puck back once they have turned. A skates with the puck along the board over the centre line and passes down into the other corner, gets it back and shoots.\n\nChange the fixed passers now and then. Run it from both long sides so the players practise both forehand and backhand. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Keep the speed up the whole way – take the passes on the move."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Turn your body before you get the puck back."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Passer: play the pass in front of the player, in their skating direction."
    }
  ],
